<section class="elysian-static-page">
  <div class="elysian-static-hero">
    <span class="elysian-static-eyebrow">Hair Care</span>
    <h1 class="elysian-static-title">FAQs</h1>
    <p class="elysian-static-intro">
      Answers to the questions we hear most about raw hair, lace, installs, and maintenance.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="elysian-faq-list">
    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>Is your hair 100% raw and unprocessed?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Yes. Our hair is single-donor, cuticle-aligned raw hair. It has not been chemically processed for color or texture — you get natural movement and longevity when cared for properly.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>How long will my extensions or wig last?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>With consistent care, most clients enjoy 1–2+ years from bundles and 6–12+ months from a well-maintained lace unit. Lifespan depends on heat use, wash frequency, and install method.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>Can I color or bleach the hair?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Raw hair can be colored, but we recommend a professional stylist. Always strand-test first and deep condition after any chemical service. Bleaching will affect longevity — treat hair gently afterward.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>How often should I wash my install?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Every 7–14 days is typical. Wash sooner if you sweat heavily, use a lot of styling product, or notice buildup at the roots or lace line.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>What products do you recommend?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Use sulfate-free shampoo, a moisturizing conditioner, leave-in conditioner, and a light serum or oil on the ends. Avoid heavy products at the lace or weft area.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>Do you offer exchanges or returns?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Please review our store policies for current return and exchange terms. Unopened, unused items in original condition may qualify — contact support with your order number for help.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="elysian-faq-item">
      <summary>How do I choose the right origin or texture?</summary>
      <div class="elysian-faq-answer rte">
        <p>Indian and Vietnamese hair tend to be silkier; Cambodian and Burmese offer more natural volume and texture. Use our Hair Quiz or reach out — we are happy to match you to your goals.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
